To mount a completely separate FastAPI app under `/subapi` with its own docs, you would follow these steps:

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/app")
def read_main():
    return {"message": "Hello World from main app"}

subapi = FastAPI()

@subapi.get("/sub")
def read_sub():
    return {"message": "Hello World from sub API"}

app.mount("/subapi", subapi)
```

This code mounts the `subapi` under `/subapi`, ensuring that its own documentation is available at `[http://127.0.0.1:8000/subapi/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8000/subapi/docs)` [3][4].
